{:kotoba.stdlib/version 1
 :kotoba.stdlib/release "0.1.0"
 :kotoba.stdlib/public-names-manifest "lang/conformance/stdlib/manifest.edn"
 :kotoba.stdlib/wbs "T4.1"
 :kotoba.stdlib/artifacts
 [{:id :core
   :path "stdlib/core.kotoba"
   :sha256 "83f3eb9c698e77f59b72e41ebb8e3270e5407c6d58354fd06c5dd69bfbea6d0b"}]
 ;; WHAT ADMITS PORTABLE LIBRARY SOURCE. The invariant has not changed --
 ;; library source is compiled WITH the program and never loaded from ambient
 ;; runtime state -- but this key named a route that does not carry it, and a
 ;; route that fails closed reads exactly like one that worked.
 :kotoba.stdlib/import-policy
 {:mode :explicit-source-path
  :cli ["compile" "--source-path"]
  :ambient-default false
  :reason "Portable library source is admitted and compiled with the program; it is never loaded from ambient runtime state. The project route resolves a CLOSED module graph from explicit source roots -- namespace to path, one file per namespace, symlink escape and cross-root ambiguity refused -- which is a stronger form of the same invariant than prepending a file: nothing enters the build that a (:require ...) in the graph did not name."
  :example "amu check <entry> --source-path <app dir> --source-path <lib dir> --jvm-free"
  :jvm-free true

  ;; `--prelude` is not a route. Measured 2026-09-01 against amu 93c4998:
  :superseded-cli
  {:flag "--prelude"
   :status :not-implemented-anywhere
   :measured
   {:as-of "2026-09-01"
    :amu "93c4998"
    :nbb-route "amu check app.kotoba --prelude lang/stdlib/core.kotoba --jvm-free exits 64: '--prelude is not implemented on this route and would be silently ignored; only the CLJS backend reads it.'"
    :jvm-route "silently ignored. kotoba.compiler.cli reads flags by name (option/options); an unrecognised one is skipped without comment, and the string \"prelude\" does not occur in that file."
    :cljs-backend "does NOT read it either, contrary to what the launcher's own refusal message says. kotoba.compiler.backend.cljs/emit takes [kir fuel]; its `prelude-forms` is the emitted fuel/quot RUNTIME prelude, not a source file. The string \"--prelude\" occurs nowhere in amu outside bin/amu's refusal and the launcher test that pins it."
    :correction "the launcher refuses for a good reason and the refusal should stand; only its stated scope is too generous. Reported, not changed here -- bin/amu belongs to kotoba-lang/amu."}}

  ;; And the honest part: naming the working route does not make this package
  ;; reachable through it. `lang/stdlib/core.kotoba` is not admissible today,
  ;; for two independent reasons, both measured 2026-09-01 against amu 93c4998.
  :artifact-reachability
  {:status :unreachable
   :blockers
   [{:id :no-namespace-form
     :evidence "the file declares no (ns ...) and no (:export ...). Requiring stdlib.core with --source-path <lang dir> is refused: 'project module requires exactly one namespace'. Adding an (ns stdlib.core (:export [...])) header to a copy got past the linker, so this is the whole of that blocker."
     :note "the diagnostic names the ENTRY module as :source, not the module that lacks the namespace, which reads as though the caller's own file is at fault."}
    {:id :empty-defrecord
     :evidence "with the header added, admission fails on (defrecord None []) with :kotoba.error/record-fields, 'record fields must be a non-empty unique bounded vector'. Isolated: a two-line file containing only (defrecord None []) and a main is refused the same way, and the same file with (defrecord Some [value]) is admitted. `amu check lang/stdlib/core.kotoba --jvm-free` alone exits 65 on it."
     :also-blocks "the prepend model this key used to name: concatenating lang/conformance/stdlib/core.kotoba ahead of lang/conformance/stdlib/basic.kotoba and checking the result fails identically, so the conformance case :portable-source-stdlib would not pass if something ran it."}]
   :consequence "the :implemented-partial disposition this package carries is not currently demonstrable by any route. Recorded rather than downgraded: which of the two blockers is a language decision (does an empty record type stay refused?) and which is a missing header is not this file's call."}

  ;; The same claim is carried elsewhere and is NOT corrected here.
  :also-claimed-in
  [{:path "lang/cli.edn"
    :at ":compile options, :id :prelude"
    :says "Explicit portable source prelude prepended before the entry source."
    :status "specified by this authority, refused by the implementation. Changing the CLI specification is a language decision, not a documentation fix."}
   {:path "lang/surface-status.edn"
    :at ":portable-source-stdlib"
    :says ":import-policy :explicit-prelude, :cli-conformance {:command \"compile --prelude\"}"
    :status "same correction due; left alone to avoid colliding with concurrent work in that file 2026-09-01."}
   {:path "lang/conformance/manifest.edn"
    :at "case :portable-source-stdlib, key :prelude"
    :status "declared and unread. Nothing in amu consumes a :prelude key from a conformance case; its runner has no occurrence of the word."}
   {:path "docs/lang/option-result-guide.md"
    :at "the Option/Result table"
    :says "Programs compiled with --prelude / conformance :prelude"
    :status "same correction due."}]}
 :kotoba.stdlib/compatibility
 {:language-profile 4
  :backends #{:compiler :kotoba-wasm :kotoba-cljs}}}
